WEBVTT

00:19.700 --> 00:22.540
Are you all right, Kasane-san?

00:22.540 --> 00:24.080
Oh, Akashi.

00:24.080 --> 00:26.380
They really went overboard, didn't they?

00:26.380 --> 00:28.710
It's not that serious.

00:28.710 --> 00:30.800
That may be so, but more so than your injuries...

00:31.880 --> 00:34.340
Thanks. I'm fine.

00:35.090 --> 00:35.930
What about you, Akashi?

00:36.390 --> 00:37.640
Nothing at all.

00:37.640 --> 00:38.640
I'm just fine.

00:40.180 --> 00:42.430
He really was a selfish guy.

00:42.430 --> 00:44.310
He sure was.

00:44.310 --> 00:49.020
Even when I would see him, all he would talk about is you.

00:50.570 --> 00:54.740
He always talked about the days when you were younger and the other good times.

00:55.200 --> 00:56.950
That's what he'd always tell me.

00:58.240 --> 01:02.580
All his life he's been rather sensitive about how other people feel.

01:02.580 --> 01:05.290
So even our father felt somewhat disturbed.

01:05.750 --> 01:11.170
And at some point, he closed his heart off
and started to reject pretty much everyone.

01:11.170 --> 01:16.300
But he used to be a kind kid that would be one step ahead and comfort friends that were sad.

01:16.800 --> 01:21.260
That's why I'm always going to be the one by his side.

01:25.270 --> 01:26.480
He really was selfish.

01:27.900 --> 01:31.230
Despite that, I'm glad I was able to meet him.

01:33.150 --> 01:36.740
And I'm glad he was my older brother.

01:39.780 --> 01:41.830
Good night, Aoshi.

01:42.580 --> 01:44.120
Sleep well.

01:45.000 --> 01:52.090
The light nearby is unseen due to its proximity and is realized after it is lost.

01:52.960 --> 01:57.220
The realization that by the time
you notice, it's already too late...

01:59.760 --> 02:02.100
Saginuma Aoshi's death has been confirmed.

02:04.970 --> 02:07.440
Apparently he fully turned into Necrometal.

02:07.440 --> 02:11.060
And the abnormally high
resonance rate was a premonition.

02:11.060 --> 02:14.570
They said if you become a LIM,
your heart can live forever...

02:14.570 --> 02:18.030
It just means that even that had limits.

02:18.030 --> 02:20.780
Then Emiru and Sasame-san might too?

02:20.780 --> 02:24.160
I can't deny the possibility that they'll share the same fate.

02:24.160 --> 02:25.540
That can't be...

02:27.210 --> 02:32.000
That day, they heard the footsteps of despair.

02:42.720 --> 02:51.060
The ink on today's graffiti runs

02:51.060 --> 03:02.070
A bicycle that has been abandoned awaits someone's return

03:02.070 --> 03:13.040
When we realized, it was up for us to choose if our existence is a replica or not

03:13.040 --> 03:17.420
Where is our proof?

03:17.420 --> 03:22.510
It's mankinds nature to come together

03:22.510 --> 03:27.560
Our love and bonds are things we can trust

03:27.560 --> 03:32.350
My sins are to be doubted

03:32.350 --> 03:38.690
The light I saw when you first held out your right hand

03:42.070 --> 03:47.540
We really are

03:56.040 --> 03:58.250
The Dark Metal

04:02.470 --> 04:07.470
Episode 21
You Will, to the Birth Cry of the End

04:07.970 --> 04:11.430
Are we going to be all right now without the Argent?

04:11.430 --> 04:13.390
It's going to be tough.

04:13.390 --> 04:14.900
That's for sure.

04:14.900 --> 04:18.770
Hey, is it completely out of commission without a LIM?

04:19.690 --> 04:25.950
It can be operated, but without a LIM, the fact
that it has a humanoid shape will only be a risk.

04:28.160 --> 04:31.660
If we have to counter the Corpse with only

04:31.660 --> 04:34.670
the two remaining machines,
we can't face it directly

04:39.590 --> 04:42.090
It was a miracle that took place
because she had a strong will.
The will to live, live on,
and fight once again...
For the sake of happiness,
instead of for the sake of revenge...

04:54.100 --> 04:55.770
Idiot!

04:55.770 --> 05:00.020
Why? Why does Emiru have to face all this?!

05:00.690 --> 05:01.940
Gimme a break!

05:01.940 --> 05:05.910
Screw these adults! All of them should just die!

05:05.910 --> 05:07.740
Emiru...

05:07.740 --> 05:10.540
Emiru is going to be happy!

05:10.540 --> 05:12.450
She just can't die!

05:22.710 --> 05:25.010
I can't be hesitating any longer.

05:31.220 --> 05:32.270
Iwato!

05:35.980 --> 05:37.310
Yo.

05:37.310 --> 05:38.600
Iwato!

05:38.600 --> 05:40.820
You're thinking of something weird right now, aren't you?

05:42.230 --> 05:44.490
Can that be?

05:44.490 --> 05:45.950
That's right.

05:45.950 --> 05:47.360
It's a piece of the Corpse.

05:47.360 --> 05:49.740
One little splash and Necrometal will appear rapidly.

05:49.740 --> 05:51.530
What nonsense are you talking about?

05:52.450 --> 05:56.960
I had a bad feeling from back when we were listening to Suzaki-san.

05:56.960 --> 05:58.670
I'm glad I came looking for you.

05:58.670 --> 06:01.000
Now, we're gonna go return that.

06:01.000 --> 06:04.050
You think we can beat the Corpse without the Reaper?

06:04.050 --> 06:05.460
It's fine!

06:05.460 --> 06:08.180
If you piloted the Reaper, you'd be the strongest, right?

06:08.180 --> 06:10.090
Don't give me this nonsense!

06:10.090 --> 06:12.050
I'm not talking nonsense!

06:10.470 --> 06:12.430
Hand it over right now!

06:12.050 --> 06:12.640
Be careful—

06:22.440 --> 06:25.650
Iwato, you're trembling...

06:25.650 --> 06:28.950
Of course I am.

06:28.950 --> 06:30.570
I'm scared of becoming a LIM...

06:30.570 --> 06:32.490
Then...

06:32.490 --> 06:36.910
But I don't want to chicken out now and end up regretting it later either.

06:37.540 --> 06:42.750
It's the worst feeling to watch Emiru
and Sasame die with regrets in my heart.

06:44.380 --> 06:45.590
I...

06:45.590 --> 06:47.210
I don't want that.

06:47.880 --> 06:51.550
I want to save Emiru and Sasame too!

06:51.550 --> 06:56.850
But I don't want to be a LIM,
and I don't want you to be one either, Iwato.

06:58.310 --> 06:59.890
Absolutely not.

07:05.940 --> 07:07.360
You...

07:07.360 --> 07:09.280
really are pretty.

07:10.990 --> 07:16.660
It's slightly relieving that you said what I couldn't because it just wasn't cool for me to say it.

07:17.790 --> 07:21.000
We really are connected, aren't we?

07:22.500 --> 07:24.090
Hey, Raika...

07:25.290 --> 07:27.250
Can you give me some courage?

07:27.960 --> 07:30.170
You can make me into a man.

07:32.260 --> 07:33.840
Absolutely not...

07:36.260 --> 07:37.560
Absolutely...

07:39.560 --> 07:40.980
That's not it.

07:44.440 --> 07:45.560
And neither is that...

07:45.560 --> 07:47.020
Please enter your password.

07:45.560 --> 07:47.020
Enter

07:47.610 --> 07:48.940
It's no good.

07:49.780 --> 07:51.200
Thanks for the hard work.

07:52.780 --> 07:53.990
Susan...

07:55.030 --> 07:56.490
I kept it a bit weak.

07:57.370 --> 07:58.870
Thanks.

07:59.620 --> 08:01.210
So, how's the planning coming along?

08:01.210 --> 08:02.540
Got something together yet?

08:02.540 --> 08:05.840
All the railroads leading to the Lightless Realm are busted.

08:06.290 --> 08:10.420
I can't be certain it's safe, but we'll have to use the highways.

08:10.420 --> 08:12.760
We're in a pretty tough situation.

08:12.760 --> 08:14.390
I see.

08:14.390 --> 08:15.590
How about you?

08:15.590 --> 08:17.600
How was that server you brought back?

08:17.600 --> 08:21.310
Almost all of the research data from 10 years ago was stored on it.

08:21.310 --> 08:26.900
But I can't find anything about the Lightless Stone or the Corpse.

08:27.440 --> 08:31.650
If there's a clue in here, it would be this, but...

08:31.650 --> 08:34.160
there's a password blocking me.

08:31.650 --> 08:34.160
Please enter your password.

08:31.650 --> 08:34.160
Enter

08:34.160 --> 08:36.450
What about Natsuiri's ID?

08:36.450 --> 08:41.330
I've tried from his birthday up to his student ID number back from his days as a student.

08:41.330 --> 08:42.410
I see...

08:43.330 --> 08:45.500
Phone numbers for candy companies?

08:45.500 --> 08:46.790
Tried that too.

08:57.340 --> 09:00.430
I'm sorry about your older brother.

09:00.430 --> 09:05.520
Kasane-san felt tormented all this time for turning Aoshi-san into a LIM.

09:06.060 --> 09:09.940
The feelings people have for each other bind them down together.

09:10.520 --> 09:15.990
No matter how much you feel for someone else, words will pass each other by.

09:15.990 --> 09:17.660
What's the meaning of this?

09:17.660 --> 09:20.490
And that leaves regrets.

09:20.490 --> 09:23.450
Both for the person that departed and the one left behind.

09:24.000 --> 09:26.710
Like me, and my older sister...

09:27.460 --> 09:28.540
Minashi...

09:29.750 --> 09:34.760
So, in order to prevent increasing
feelings of this sort from now on, I...

09:35.260 --> 09:37.800
We have to become connected.

09:37.800 --> 09:39.600
So, Akashi, you and I—

09:39.600 --> 09:40.350
Stop it!

09:41.220 --> 09:43.100
There's nothing to fear.

09:43.100 --> 09:45.310
I told you to stop it.

09:45.310 --> 09:47.310
Even if we passed each other by...

09:47.940 --> 09:49.980
Big Brother was content when he died.

09:50.520 --> 09:52.230
Kasane-san was too.

09:55.240 --> 09:59.570
What the two of them had between them was something very special.

10:00.320 --> 10:03.080
And those feelings continued to grow for years,

10:03.080 --> 10:06.830
by not understanding, or misunderstanding...

10:06.830 --> 10:10.130
That was how they ultimately arrived at those feelings.

10:11.630 --> 10:13.300
You haven't changed at all.

10:13.750 --> 10:17.590
That's nothing more than your selfish imagination!

10:18.470 --> 10:24.770
Because you were clamming your heart shut,
neither Tsugumi nor Sasame could understand you,

10:24.770 --> 10:26.350
and so they had a tough time.

10:27.140 --> 10:31.440
If you could even muster some courage to connect to us, everyone would be saved.

10:31.440 --> 10:33.570
I can't think that to be the case.

10:37.440 --> 10:39.070
I see.

10:39.070 --> 10:40.780
So you're that much of a lost cause, Akashi.

10:51.630 --> 10:52.710
What?

10:53.340 --> 10:54.840
You're kidding.

11:06.430 --> 11:08.060
Tsugumi...

11:08.060 --> 11:09.390
It's you, isn't it?

11:30.660 --> 11:32.000
Akashi...

11:33.790 --> 11:35.790
Let's make up.

11:38.590 --> 11:40.050
Akashi...

11:42.980 --> 11:47.070
It was roughly two hours ago that we
observed the anomaly in the Lightless Realm.

11:47.070 --> 11:50.230
And as you can see, it is continuing to expand.

11:50.660 --> 11:52.350
If it keeps up at its current speed,

11:52.830 --> 11:57.900
the entire Kujicho area including this
facility will be swallowed up in five days' time.

11:58.460 --> 12:04.450
The government has already ordered evacuation
of all Self-Defense Force members and IX employees.

12:04.450 --> 12:07.960
The few civilians that stayed are in the
process of gradually evacuating as well.

12:04.450 --> 12:05.920
Shop will be closed temporarily.
Thank you very much for your
patronage for such a long time.

12:09.500 --> 12:14.830
Moments ago, the executives of IX
agreed to follow the government's orders.

12:14.830 --> 12:16.190
Hold on.

12:16.190 --> 12:20.400
If we abandon this base, won't we lose all
means to fight against the Lightless Realm?

12:20.400 --> 12:24.180
What would happen to the research to turn Emiru and Sasame-san back to normal?

12:24.610 --> 12:25.780
Yes.

12:25.780 --> 12:29.060
That's why we've decided to stay here.

12:29.060 --> 12:31.390
But we can't force you to do so as well.

12:31.390 --> 12:35.100
In other words, you have priority in evacuating.

12:35.100 --> 12:38.900
Nobody will blame you if you evacuated immediately.

12:39.670 --> 12:41.320
You can do as you wish.

12:42.420 --> 12:43.190
What will it be?

12:44.420 --> 12:47.340
None of us would run after coming this far.

12:47.340 --> 12:48.760
Exactly.

12:48.760 --> 12:50.830
I want to stay too.

12:51.930 --> 12:52.960
Thank you.

12:53.970 --> 12:55.250
We appreciate it.

12:55.250 --> 12:58.460
About that server Natsuiri had...

13:02.150 --> 13:09.600
As long as I listen to what Susan said,
I'm sure the password has something to do with her...

13:20.230 --> 13:20.270
The days of a humble researcher.
There aren't many updates, I'm sorry...

13:21.250 --> 13:22.850
Oh, her blog is still up.

13:24.530 --> 13:26.950
Her last entry was the day that she went back to the island.

13:29.410 --> 13:29.450
Miraculous meeting!

13:30.090 --> 13:33.340
Mr. N, I met someone at today's research presentation

13:33.340 --> 13:36.850
I think he may be someone who
can open the paths to my dreams.

13:35.620 --> 13:35.660
One step towards my dream

13:36.850 --> 13:40.750
I am going to start assisting Mr. N on his research.

13:41.770 --> 13:48.450
Finally! Finally! Mr. N's research has been approved! I'm so happy! I'm so happy!

13:47.550 --> 13:47.590
Got a heart

13:47.590 --> 13:47.630
Congratulations!

13:59.980 --> 14:00.020
I can't prepare in time

14:00.410 --> 14:03.390
I have to hurry making preparations to go back to the island.

14:03.390 --> 14:08.450
I can't buy the ingredients for Mr. N's
favorite Napolitan spaghetti on the island!

14:09.260 --> 14:10.710
Napolitan...

14:15.590 --> 14:16.870
I got in!

14:17.550 --> 14:21.840
The file concerning the Necrometal phenomenon was indeed in there.

14:23.560 --> 14:28.650
It's a theoretical model of how the Lightless
Realm was turning materials into Necrometal.

14:28.650 --> 14:31.550
I guess you could say it's the heart of the matter.

14:31.550 --> 14:36.180
The conclusion was that the information about the matter's existence was being directly overwritten.

14:39.020 --> 14:43.830
Kasane, can you keep with just
the important points and simplify?

14:43.830 --> 14:48.170
Well, in other words, if we can shed light on that information about its existence,

14:48.170 --> 14:51.280
we might be able to revert the transition into Necrometal.

14:51.960 --> 14:53.120
Is that really true?

14:53.120 --> 14:54.390
Yes.

14:54.390 --> 14:58.580
But to do that, it is indeed necessary to do analysis of the Lightless Stone.

14:59.260 --> 15:01.790
So it all winds back to defeating the Corpse, after all.

15:10.110 --> 15:11.320
We have to do it.

15:12.570 --> 15:14.030
Even without the Reaper.

15:20.510 --> 15:23.730
And so, I was think of an operation against the Corpse.

15:23.730 --> 15:27.920
First, we'll use the Tomei Highway
that suffered relatively little damage

15:27.920 --> 15:30.900
and have the 2nd and 3rd machines enter the Lightless Realm.

15:32.160 --> 15:35.420
Right after making contact with the Corpse, avoid contact,

15:35.420 --> 15:38.090
then retreat back outside the Lightless Realm.

15:38.090 --> 15:43.270
There, Iwato and Raika aboard Vesses and
Akashi aboard the Argent will be standing by.

15:43.270 --> 15:44.350
The Argent?

15:44.350 --> 15:45.800
Will it be all right?

15:46.310 --> 15:48.480
I can't expect high mobility,

15:48.480 --> 15:52.690
but to make sure we finish the Corpse, it's better if we have three MA-Vesses.

15:52.690 --> 15:55.940
But this means Iwato and Raika
needs to properly back them up.

15:55.940 --> 15:57.470
Understood.

15:57.910 --> 16:01.690
Everyone will work together in order to nab it.

16:01.690 --> 16:04.250
The operation will start tomorrow at noon.

16:04.250 --> 16:06.080
It will be a fierce battle.

16:06.080 --> 16:08.750
Until then, make sure to get enough rest.

16:08.750 --> 16:10.000
Um...

16:10.000 --> 16:10.900
What?

16:13.670 --> 16:15.780
No, never mind.

16:15.780 --> 16:16.820
I see.

16:16.820 --> 16:18.020
Then, with that, you're all dismissed.

16:26.310 --> 16:29.650
Nothing less from Suzaki-san. That was a perfect strategy.

16:29.650 --> 16:30.410
Yes...

16:38.900 --> 16:40.210
I'm so pathetic...

16:41.700 --> 16:43.490
I become like this at the last minute?

16:44.120 --> 16:45.040
Iwato...

16:46.060 --> 16:48.690
This is a time where we need a LIM...

16:49.540 --> 16:52.050
Dammit, I can't do it after all!

16:55.590 --> 16:57.410
Iwato, you're fine like that.

16:58.490 --> 17:00.520
I'll bear it together with you...

17:01.420 --> 17:02.390
So...

17:04.180 --> 17:05.120
Raika...

17:27.330 --> 17:28.190
I'm...

17:28.970 --> 17:31.950
Let's stay together, Iwato.

17:36.630 --> 17:39.050
We'll be together when we bear the burden of sin.

17:47.180 --> 17:48.760
Let's go, Sasame.

17:49.420 --> 17:50.820
Tsugumi is waiting.

17:52.800 --> 17:54.020
Minashi...

17:55.810 --> 17:57.380
Planning on going somewhere?

17:57.380 --> 17:58.940
Yeah.

17:58.940 --> 18:01.850
Sasame and I are going to see Tsugumi together.

18:02.280 --> 18:05.310
It's reckless to go against the Corpse with just Gueules.

18:05.870 --> 18:07.930
I'm not going to fight.

18:07.930 --> 18:09.700
I'm going to go save Tsugumi.

18:10.330 --> 18:12.730
Because it's something you can't do, Akashi.

18:13.500 --> 18:16.370
Akashi, you don't understand things about us.

18:16.980 --> 18:18.720
No matter how many words we pile up—

18:18.720 --> 18:19.710
Wait!

18:19.710 --> 18:24.040
Are you saying you can get rid of
Tsugumi's grudges and her loneliness?

18:24.040 --> 18:27.700
See, you don't understand anything at all.

18:28.350 --> 18:32.500
Tsugumi is trembling at a point past grudges and loneliness.

18:33.190 --> 18:37.470
It was because we met you guys, and got completely separated.

18:38.750 --> 18:41.720
And once again, we're going to connect back into one.

18:42.450 --> 18:43.920
It's a simple concept.

18:47.070 --> 18:50.580
So just connecting automatically
means you understand each other?

18:50.580 --> 18:51.330
I don't think that's—

18:54.840 --> 18:55.770
Hey!

18:56.940 --> 18:59.910
You can't save Tsugumi or Sasame!

19:01.260 --> 19:02.280
Stop it, Minashi!

19:02.280 --> 19:04.430
I have to do this!

19:08.750 --> 19:10.880
Let's go, Sasame.

19:17.900 --> 19:20.000
Are you going to reject me?

19:20.000 --> 19:21.720
Tsugumi will scold you for that.

19:23.860 --> 19:25.560
Good girl.

19:29.810 --> 19:32.520
Stop it, Minashi! That's dangerous!

19:32.520 --> 19:33.760
Minashi!

19:34.310 --> 19:36.010
Don't go, Sasame!

19:45.490 --> 19:47.350
Sasame! Minashi!

19:47.350 --> 19:47.990
Dammit!

19:54.560 --> 19:55.940
Minashi, what are you doing?

19:55.940 --> 19:57.410
Come back! Minashi!

20:01.570 --> 20:03.720
What are you thinking, Minashi?

20:04.990 --> 20:08.720
Suzaki-san, Minashi is headed
to the Lightless Realm by himself.

20:09.240 --> 20:11.010
No, he's not alone.

20:11.010 --> 20:12.450
He's together with Sasame...

20:13.410 --> 20:14.440
His objective?

20:14.440 --> 20:16.980
Something about becoming one with Tsugumi.

20:16.980 --> 20:18.200
I just don't get it at all.

20:18.940 --> 20:21.490
Akashi, continue your pursuit.

20:21.490 --> 20:23.840
We'll head over there now as well.

20:23.840 --> 20:24.920
Roger.

20:26.660 --> 20:30.250
Compared to a MA-Vess, it doesn't move nearly as nimbly.

20:32.300 --> 20:33.830
Of all times...

20:35.640 --> 20:39.690
Why is Minashi acting so selfishly?

20:39.690 --> 20:41.010
Complain later.

20:41.450 --> 20:42.810
We'll make sure to catch up to him!

20:42.810 --> 20:43.720
Yes!
Yeah!

20:46.720 --> 20:50.530
Stop him before he enters the
Lightless Realm, no matter what!

20:50.530 --> 20:51.460
Roger!

20:55.830 --> 20:57.310
An Admonition?

20:57.310 --> 20:59.460
We can't go any further with that thing!

20:59.460 --> 21:00.960
Support Akashi!

21:00.960 --> 21:02.130
Uh, sure!

21:03.070 --> 21:04.500
On it!

21:04.500 --> 21:05.420
Geez!

21:17.510 --> 21:18.530
Everyone...

21:29.620 --> 21:30.640
You saved me.

21:31.150 --> 21:34.350
But we're really far behind Minashi now.

21:34.350 --> 21:35.240
Dammit!

21:36.060 --> 21:37.490
We should hurry.

21:37.490 --> 21:38.500
Yeah.

21:43.000 --> 21:44.050
Tsugumi...

21:45.010 --> 21:47.490
We should become one once again.

21:48.510 --> 21:50.240
Just like when we were kids.

21:52.010 --> 21:52.860
No...

21:53.540 --> 21:57.470
Our connection now should be stronger than it was back then.

22:07.320 --> 22:08.520
Sasame...

22:10.610 --> 22:11.600
Hey...

22:13.780 --> 22:17.000
Akashi, can you hear me?

22:17.830 --> 22:19.100
You're...

22:19.100 --> 22:20.390
What the?

22:20.390 --> 22:21.680
What's going on?

22:23.750 --> 22:27.320
Don't you be getting in the way of my solitude.

22:28.750 --> 22:31.660
Man, how disgusting.

22:56.430 --> 23:00.480
You lose your mind, you crash; a nervous breakdown

23:00.480 --> 23:05.230
You feel an urge inside, you crush; there's no escape now

23:05.230 --> 23:10.110
You try to change your life, you jump another let down

23:10.110 --> 23:12.700
